    "body": "Spent a morning figuring out what I can do on my own: https://codepen.io/eeeps/pen/MWJyJKG?editors=1111. Not sure what I have is correct...\r\n\r\n(This would be a lot cleaner/easier with something like https://github.com/w3c/css-houdini-drafts/issues/798)\r\n\r\nIn any case, turning a [source-size-value](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#source-size-value) into an integer representing the resolved `sizes` value in `px` isn't trivial, and it would be nice if the browser, which has already done the conversion as part of `srcset` selection, exposed the value directly.\r\n\r\nA couple of other thoughts:\r\n\r\n- If we get more-complicated `sizes`, through either [height-constrained `srcset` selection](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2973), or [container-relative units w/in `sizes`](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/5889#issuecomment-777918275), it'll be even nicer for the browser to expose this.\r\n- I'm working on a Responsive Images Client Hints polyfill; this would be very useful for that, too.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
