    "updated_at": "2023-06-27T23:45:29Z",
    "body": "I think [sizes=auto](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/8008) (and its [emerging complexities](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9448#issuecomment-1609960596)) makes this even more important. Developers are going to assume that sizes=auto is doing the right thing when if they're not careful, it won't. cc) @zcorpan \r\n\r\nI'm imagining a Lighthouse test or whatever that can check if sizes.currentSizes === img.clientWidth onload for imgs with sizes=auto. If not, there's been some hard-to-see problem.",
